# Bot2 changes the text of Bot1's Grist spell on the stack with Artificial Evolution, Insect to Elf (CR 612.1; the effect
# goes on applying to the permanent it becomes, CR 400.7a). Grist's +1 then makes a 1/1 black and green Elf token
# (CR 612.4) and "if an Insect card was milled" asks for an Elf card: Llanowar Elves, milled first, repeats the process
# and puts a loyalty counter on Grist (3 + 1 + 1 = 5), and the Island milled next ends it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Grist, the Hunger Tide
Island x4
Llanowar Elves
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Artificial Evolution
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Stack.Grist, the Hunger Tide)
Bot2.Modes(Insect)
Bot2.Modes(Elf)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
[Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Activate(Ability: +1)
[Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Counters.Loyalty = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Subtypes = Grist
Bot1.Battlefield.Elf Token#1.Subtypes = Elf
Bot1.Battlefield.Elf Token#2.Subtypes = Elf
Bot1.Battlefield.Elf Token#1.Colors = Black; Green
Bot1.Graveyard = Island; Llanowar Elves
